# The `litigate build` arguments the repository's generated packs,
# packs/links.json, generated clock fragments and named scenarios are built
# from (DESIGN §11.4, SPEC §9.4): one argument per line, `#` comments.
# build.rs builds them into this crate at compile time; `just lit-sync`
# writes the same build to target/lit-build/ for inspection. lit/core and
# lit/examples are library/teaching packages and emit no pack.
lit/cafc
lit/cofc
lit/frap
lit/bap8
lit/frcp
lit/frcrimp
lit/itc
lit/mpep
lit/ptab
lit/ttab
lit/links
cases/cofc-1498-patent-case.case
cases/cofc-bid-protest.case
cases/frcp-civil-case.case
cases/ptab-ipr-defense.case
cases/ttab-opposition-applicant-defense.case
# `--pack-file ID=STEM` keeps a legacy file name where it is not the id.
--pack-file
cafc=cafc-federal-circuit
--pack-file
cofc=cofc-court-of-federal-claims
